===Etymology===
A Shetlandic and Orcadian alteration of ''[[trow]]'', most likely influenced by an unattested {{etyl|nrn|en}} {{m|nrn|*drog||malevolent [undead] being}}. ''Trow'' is derived from {{etyl|nrn|en}} {{m|nrn|troll}}, or otherwise from {{etyl|non|en}} {{m|non|trǫll}}. L-vocalisation occurred in the early 15th century in Middle Scots, so "''[[troll|trolly]] [[knoll|knolls]]''" probably became "''trowie knowes''" around this time. The supposed Norn {{m|nrn|*drog}} would have been derived from {{etyl|non|en}} {{m|non|draugr}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|drow}}

# {{lb|en|fantasy|_|RPG|countable}} A member of a fictional race of dark [[elf|elves]] in various fantasy settings, such as ''[[w:Dungeons & Dragons|Dungeons & Dragons]]''.
# {{lb|en|fantasy|_|RPG|uncountable}} A fictional [[constructed language]] <!-- invented by ? --> spoken by the Drow. <!--capital D?-->
# {{lb|en|rare|mythology|countable}} A [[trow]]; a member of a race of folkloric beings from [[Orkney]] and [[Shetland]]; cognate to the Scandinavian [[troll]]<ref>[http://www.dsl.ac.uk/dsl/getent4.php?plen=11075&startset=44442733&query=TROW&fhit=trowe&dregion=entry&dtext=snd#fhit Dictionary of the Scots Language]</ref>.

